// A function reaches a top-level declaration as a global: `g` is the program's
// global `g0`, which `f` writes and reads with `SetGlobal` and `GetGlobal`. `f`
// captures nothing, so its declaration loads it as a plain constant with
// `LoadK`, with no `Closure`.
// compile: analysed
let g = 1;
fn f() { g = 2; g }
